.TH CUTSTEP 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
CutStep \- One instruction in a cutscene script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqcutscene.h\(dq
.ft B
typedef struct CutStep {
  CutKind     kind;
  float       duration;
  Vec2       *actor;
  Vec2        to;
  const char *speaker, *text;
  void      (*fn)(Engine *, void *ctx);
} CutStep;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
One instruction in a cutscene script. Write scripts with the CUT_* macros rather than filling fields by hand. A script with no actors can be a static const array: static const CutStep intro[] = { CUT_FADE_IN_S(1), CUT_SAY_LINE("Cat", "Finally, a warm spot."), CUT_DO(give_key), CUT_FADE_OUT_S(1) };. A script that moves an entity in GameState is filled in at run time, because the entity's address is not a compile\-time constant: static CutStep walk[2]; walk[0] = (CutStep)CUT_MOVE_TO(&g\->player.pos, 200, 100, 2); walk[1] = (CutStep)CUT_SAY_LINE("Cat", "Here."); (each macro expands to a brace initializer, so a cast turns it into a compound literal). Which fields matter depends on kind.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B kind
what the step does
.TP
.B duration
seconds, for WAIT, MOVE and the fades
.TP
.B actor
pointer to the Vec2 to move, for MOVE; must stay valid for the cutscene's life (an entity in GameState is fine; a local is not)
.TP
.B to
destination for MOVE
.TP
.B speaker
name for SAY, or NULL
.TP
.B text
line for SAY
.TP
.B fn
callback for CALL; receives the Engine and the ctx passed to cutscene_start()
.SH MODULE
cutscene (src/engine/cutscene/cutscene.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR CutKind (3),
.BR cutscene_start (3),
.BR CUT_WAIT_S (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
